Better handling of keys that report no proper code

• A key's identity is now fixed when you press it and kept until you release it. Recomputing it per event could file the release under a different key, so the press never completed and the key silently did nothing.
• Assigning a key now shows the raw numbers it received, and pauses so you can read them.
• If Android lists SideKeys as enabled while nothing is running, the app says so.
• DuraSpeed handling rebuilt on better information.
